package:
  name: hdllint.vlt
  desc: Verilator lint integration (`verilator --lint-only`)
  doc: |
    Verilator as a lint tool. It is the reference backend for this library:
    open source, already present in most flows, and fast enough to run on
    every change.

    What it sees: the synthesis subset, elaborated. That is what makes its
    high-value checks possible -- width truncation and expansion, inferred
    latches, unused and undriven signals, blocking-assignment ordering
    races -- and it is also its limit. It cannot parse class-based
    testbench code, so it implements the `Rtl` family and no other.

    `verilator --lint-only -Wno-fatal` is always used. `-Wno-fatal` is not
    a relaxation: it stops Verilator from cutting the run short once
    warnings accumulate, so one run reports everything. Whether the run
    fails is decided by `fail_on:` after waivers and the baseline have been
    applied.

    Verilator is the property of its respective owners.

  imports:
  - name: hdllint

  tasks:
  - export: Rtl
    uses: hdllint.Rtl
    desc: Runs `verilator --lint-only` and reports normalized findings
    doc: |
      The `hdllint.Rtl` family task with `tools:` pinned to Verilator.
      Identical in every other respect -- same waivers, same baseline, same
      reports.

      Use this when a flow wants Verilator specifically; use `hdllint.Rtl`
      when it wants whatever lint tools are available.

      ```yaml
      - name: lint
        uses: hdllint.vlt.Rtl
        needs: [rtl]
        with:
          top: [wb_dma_top]
          profile: strict
      ```

      Profiles map to Verilator flags as:

      | profile   | flags                  |
      |-----------|------------------------|
      | `basic`   | (Verilator's defaults) |
      | `default` | `-Wall`                |
      | `strict`  | `-Wall -Wpedantic`     |
    with:
      tools:
        type: list
        value: [vlt]
